# Auth: run top to bottom. REST Client keeps the token cookie between requests.
# Passwords come from api/.env (requests/.env is a symlink to it).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@origin = http://localhost:5174
@json = application/json

### 1. Sign up a new reader -> 201, Set-Cookie token (HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict), no token in the body
# Change the username on every run, or expect 409 the second time.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "new_reader", "password": "a-long-password-123" }

### 2. Same username again -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "new_reader", "password": "a-long-password-123" }

### 3. Invalid sign-up data -> 422 with details
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "No Spaces!", "password": "short" }

### 4. Log in as author1 -> 200, Set-Cookie, body { user, expiresAt }
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "author1", "password": "{{$dotenv AUTHOR_PASSWORD}}" }

### 5. Who am I (uses the stored cookie) -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 6. Wrong password -> 401 "Invalid username or password"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "author1", "password": "wrong-password" }

### 7. Unknown user -> 401 with the same message as the wrong password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "nobody_here", "password": "wrong-password" }

### 8. CSRF guard: write without Origin -> 403 "Origin not allowed"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "author1", "password": "{{$dotenv AUTHOR_PASSWORD}}" }

### 9. CSRF guard: write from an unknown origin -> 403 "Origin not allowed"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: http://evil.example
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "author1", "password": "{{$dotenv AUTHOR_PASSWORD}}" }

### 10. CSRF guard: write without X-Requested-With -> 403 "Missing request header"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "username": "author1", "password": "{{$dotenv AUTHOR_PASSWORD}}" }

### 11. CSRF guard: browser marks the request as cross-site -> 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client
Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site

{ "username": "author1", "password": "{{$dotenv AUTHOR_PASSWORD}}" }

### 12. Malformed JSON -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "author1",

### 13. Log out -> 204, Set-Cookie with an expired token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

### 14. Who am I after logging out -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 15. Rate limit: send this one more than 10 times in 15 minutes -> 429
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "author1", "password": "wrong-password" }
